{"id": "EUVD-2026-93138", "enisaUuid": "cd322721-afa7-320d-bd91-ff93e45c1d63", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmmc: mxcmmc: cancel data work and watchdog on remove\n\nmxcmci_remove() frees the host through the devm tail, but neither it nor\nmmc_remove_host() drains the driver's own asynchronous state.\nhost->watchdog, a 10 s timer armed on the DMA path in mxcmci_setup_data(),\nis deleted only by the DMA- and IRQ-complete paths, which the remove path\ndoes not explicitly drain; it can therefore fire after the host is freed\nand dereference it in mxcmci_watchdog().  host->datawork, armed from the\nIRQ handler on the PIO path, is not cancelled by the remove path either.\n\nFree the devm-registered IRQ, then cancel datawork and delete the watchdog\nin mxcmci_remove(), before dma_release_channel().  Freeing the IRQ first\nkeeps a trailing handler from re-arming datawork between the cancel and\nthe host free.  Both callbacks are non-self-rearming.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:41", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/740f595f8ad678cb4d79f13edd12851df2492bdd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3641afe6ee76d852834a34ef0669eefced32752", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/314966b490323bdcfd3162a1398b00e587e0ced4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ae10838a7cdf0e54caa9d0a4f488704fd04e7f01", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a1ff367e0dc961d73707add508a95df5c3509bd1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23383e0578b58ba2dc0730cf9f7806bd66bf859a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2948c4232209e87c861a680f20f1e3cf8a57fec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3a421c82412344022982d5b91ba23194a0a6f29"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3899-r8v9-5w9h", "CVE-2026-98210"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09bbffe3-a16f-308a-a4ab-d22b5981e4f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "1c299756-3223-34cb-b3f0-47ac0b2a5022", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "25a5a126-4c4a-31bb-b390-732b7fffddd5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f6ad0a481342223b2e7ae9f55b154e14f1391ada <ae10838a7cdf0e54caa9d0a4f488704fd04e7f01"}, {"id": "2de6fc3a-e44d-387a-90af-f25477654ed1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f6ad0a481342223b2e7ae9f55b154e14f1391ada <d3641afe6ee76d852834a34ef0669eefced32752"}, {"id": "3bc37290-6ad1-388c-abc1-7309832847e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "408a9841-34e7-381b-a65b-c9f8e5dfef6c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.7"}, {"id": "45fa74cc-b03f-34d0-8f46-02749f6450bc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f6ad0a481342223b2e7ae9f55b154e14f1391ada <d3a421c82412344022982d5b91ba23194a0a6f29"}, {"id": "5aacde4e-bf16-35e8-a75c-45da295b94ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f6ad0a481342223b2e7ae9f55b154e14f1391ada <740f595f8ad678cb4d79f13edd12851df2492bdd"}, {"id": "5f97c4e9-cdb1-3906-8d73-7078a1aebd64", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "673bef62-6267-3676-9ab9-37223f700dcd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "72a908de-6050-335f-9029-635a77c494dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "7a600ed3-298a-3e32-bffe-77bc9f83528a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f6ad0a481342223b2e7ae9f55b154e14f1391ada <314966b490323bdcfd3162a1398b00e587e0ced4"}, {"id": "7fc8fc76-ad6a-33e1-a41d-3889ff6bc